                <pb facs="0387" n="381" sameAs="frus:frus1942v02/pg381"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/24340: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Consul General at Algiers (Cole)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-09-23T18:00:00-04:00">September 23,
                            1942—6 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>284. From Murphy. Your 613, September 18, 1 p.m. There has been a delay in this
                    matter which I shall explain on return. Arrangement should be possible early in
                    October. [Murphy.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
